            <ArticleTitle>Hydatid disease: a rare cause of pelvic pain (2008: 5b).</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1757-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s00330-008-0917-x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a case of hydatid disease as a rare cause of pelvic pain. Although the involvement of pelvic bones makes diagnosis challenging, characteristic imaging findings of the cysts in the other tissues highly suggest the diagnosis of hydatid disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
